            <ArticleTitle>Gastroduodenal tolerability of medium dose enteric-coated aspirin: a placebo controlled endoscopic study of a new enteric-coated formulation versus regular formulation in healthy volunteers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We compared, in a cross-over study, the toxicity of 300 mg enteric-coated aspirin with regular aspirin used for the prevention of cardiovascular events. In terms of endoscopic haemorrhagic lesions, enteric-coated aspirin is less gastrotoxic than regular aspirin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
